id     = "voice-letters-noise"
about  = """Per-letter text motion and noise (eval-coverage-5; design.md
"Text effects": `letters { y: 2 * wave(1s, phase: index * 0.1) }`, "Time
signals": `noise(x)`): a voice-input chip in a bar whose "Listening" label
ripples letter by letter and whose mic dot trembles on `noise(t * 3)`. The
listening ends and the chip leaves; started again, it ripples from its own
start (a new chip, a new clock); with the desktop's reduced motion turned on
the letters and the dot stand at t = 0 (each letter keeps its own `index`,
decisions.md m4-scene) and the bar rests where the reduced twin does."""
screen = { width = 300, height = 120, scale = 1.0 }
hz     = 60

=== shell.strand
state listening = false
bar Top {
  height: 30; bg: #1e1e2e
  row { height: 30; pad: 0, 10; gap: 6; align: center
    if listening {
      row { id: chip; height: 22; pad: 0, 8; gap: 6; align: center; radius: 11; bg: #313244
        enter { opacity: 0; scale: 0.9 }
        box { id: mic; width: 8; height: 8; radius: 4; bg: #f38ba8; x: 1.5 * noise(t * 3) }
        text "Listening" { id: label; color: #cdd6f4
          letters { y: 2 * wave(1s, phase: index * 0.1) } }
      }
    }
    spacer {}
    text "12:30" { id: clock; color: #cdd6f4 }
  }
}

=== steps
rest
mark listen
intend #chip enters
set listening true
wait 600
mark stop
intend #chip exits
set listening false
rest
mark listen-again
intend #chip enters
set listening true
wait 400
mark reduce
reduce-motion on
rest
expect still #clock
